00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:29.900
Now, if you want to, do, you know, a little
bit of multiplication.

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:30.900
The odds of Trump winning twice in a row with
29 percent likelihood is about eight percent.

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:31.900
This is like flipping a coin.

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:32.900
If you flip a coin once, the odds of heads
are 50 percent.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:33.900
If after that first flip, you flip it a second
time.

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:34.900
The odds of heads on that one flip are still
50 percent.

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:35.900
But if in advance I say to you, what are the
odds of heads twice in a row?

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:36.900
You multiply point five times, point five,
and you get 25 percent.

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:37.900
Similarly, if Trump's odds really were twenty
nine percent in 2016 and they're 29 percent

00:06:37.900 --> 00:06:38.900
now in the abstract, the odds of winning twice
with 29 percent odds are about eight percent.

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:39.900
